## Important Data-Quality Notes

### Net Worth Discrepancy — Please Read
The value reported in the table for "Net worth" (**₹1,218.86 crore**) corresponds specifically to the **Reserves & Surplus** line item (NL-10 schedule), which is the figure that aligns with how "Net Worth" is referenced within the NL-20 ratio calculations. However, a more complete net-worth figure — inclusive of Share Capital (₹972.39 crore, per NL-8) — would be:

- **Net Worth (Share Capital + Reserves & Surplus) ≈ ₹2,191.25 crore**

This is cross-validated by back-solving the NL-20 "Gross Direct Premium to Net Worth" ratio of 0.88x: ₹1,931.12 cr GWP ÷ 0.88 ≈ **₹2,194 crore**, confirming the fuller net-worth figure sits in the **~₹2,191–2,194 crore** range. Analysts consolidating this data should use the full ₹2,191.25 crore figure rather than the Reserves & Surplus-only line shown in the table.

### Underwriting Performance Deterioration
- The **Combined ratio of 101%** for Q1FY25 (versus 92% in Q1FY24 per the same disclosure) signals a clear underwriting deterioration, driven primarily by the **Claims ratio jumping to 67%** from 56% a year earlier.
- This is consistent with an **Operating Loss of ₹(21.98) crore** in Q1FY25 (per NL-1), a sharp reversal from an **Operating Profit of ₹77.25 crore** in Q1FY24.
- Despite the underwriting loss, **PAT remained positive at ₹83.16 crore**, cushioned by investment income of ₹78.05 crore (interest, dividend, and rent) plus adjustments from brought-forward reserves.

### Structural Data Gaps
- **Retail health GWP split** and **Retail health market share** are not disclosed in the IRDAI NL format — the disclosure only breaks premium out by Health/PA/Travel segment, not by Retail vs. Group within Health.
- **Blended investment yield** is not disclosed as a single portfolio figure; NL-31 only provides category/instrument-level yields (ranging ~1.3–2.0% for the quarter), not an aggregated portfolio yield.
- **IFRS-basis PAT and Claims ratio** are not applicable/disclosed — Care Health Insurance reports exclusively under the statutory IGAAP/Ind AS framework in this filing; no parallel IFRS figures are published.

### Sourcing Rationale
Since Care Health Insurance is unlisted, no standalone "Investor Presentation Q1FY25" exists publicly — all figures were sourced from the single mandatorily-published statutory filing, which serves as both the headline (GWP/PAT/ratios) and the granular (NWP/NEP/EoM/Net worth/AUM) source in this case.</ans>
